  {
   "id": 1376,
   "q": 12,
   "section": "Physics",
   "text": "A ray of light passes from air into a glass slab with a refractive index of 1.5. If the angle of incidence is 30 degrees, what is the angle of refraction?",
   "options": [
    {
     "label": "A",
     "text": "19.5 degrees",
     "correct": true
    },
    {
     "label": "B",
     "text": "20 degrees",
     "correct": false
    },
    {
     "label": "C",
     "text": "45 degrees",
     "correct": false
    },
    {
     "label": "D",
     "text": "60 degrees",
     "correct": false
    }
   ],
   "solution": "Using Snell&#39;s law, n1 sin(θ1) = n2 sin(θ2), where n1 = 1 (air) and n2 = 1.5 (glass). Rearranging the equation to solve for θ2, we get sin(θ2) = (n1 / n2) * sin(θ1) = (1 / 1.5) * sin(30) = (2/3) * 0.5 = 1/3. Then θ2 = arcsin(1/3) ≈ 19.5 degrees."
  },
